The plate is roughly 24 cm wide, so it is probably a dinner or side plate. It holds 5 roasted potato pieces (or possibly turnip), each about 4-5 cm across and 2-3 cm thick. At roughly 25-30 g per piece, that comes to about 130-150 g in total.

Roasted potato is about 1.1-1.5 kcal/g, so with a little oil the total is about 150-180 kcal. If the pieces are turnip or radish, the energy would be lower. They look like potato, so I'll use 150 kcal and 130 g.

